  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-22T06:36:34.433Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I am writing to provide feedback regarding the microphone behavior in the VRChat iOS app.\n\nWhile I would like to play musical instruments within VRChat, it appears that the iOS system-level noise cancellation is forcibly enabled, and I am unable to disable it. Although the option to change the microphone mode exists in the iOS settings, it is currently unselectable while the app is running.\n\nAs a result, the sound of my instruments is being filtered out as background noise. I would appreciate it if the development team could investigate this and consider supporting the \"Standard\" or \"Wide Spectrum\" microphone modes to allow for original sound input.\n\nThank you for your hard work on the mobile version.",
